a, Kabue, Buloba, Kapindu, Kapala, Kasengulu, Cimvuluila, Nyemvua, Ndekeluka, Kambaja, Lupandu Luetu)","evidence":"Densely populated peri-urban belt adjoining Mbuji-Mayi, administered by the state with PNC commissariats/sub-commissariats; no armed group is reported to hold territory. Insecurity consists of urban banditry (kuluna), diamond-digging disputes and occasional political unrest handled by PNC and other state services. Not verified with fresh sources in this run (web search budget exhausted, search sites blocked by egress proxy).","unit":"CD8209-katanda","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-anr","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}]}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD8209-katanda":"Katanda territory (Kasai-Oriental), east of Mbuji-Mayi, is state-administered with no known armed group holding territory. The Tshilenge/Citenge urban area and the neighbourhoods bordering Mbuji-Mayi are policed by the PNC with ANR and some FARDC presence; rural Tshitenge and Bibanga secteurs rely on PNC posts and customary chiefs. Violence is mostly banditry, land/chieftaincy and artisanal diamond-mining disputes. Live web research was unavailable in this run, so the assessment rests on background knowledge and default state presence, with limited confidence."}}